{"type": "tool_call", "n": 66, "ts": 1790148671.069498, "tool": "submit_memo", "args": {"text": "US MARCH 2026 OPERATING EXPENSE FLUX VS. FEBRUARY\nPrepared: 2026-04-03\n\nSUMMARY\nThree expense lines moved more than 10% AND more than $5,000:\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n1. HOSTING & INFRASTRUCTURE (Account 5000)\n   February: $31,301.80\n   March:    $40,948.20\n   Change:   +$9,646.40 (+30.8%)\n\nDRIVERS:\n\u2022 JE-00258 (3/14/26): Stackline Cloud one-time data migration (SC-M-2203)\n  Amount: $9,800.00 - \u2713 SUPPORTED\n  \n\u2022 JE-00232 (3/3/26): Stackline Cloud production infrastructure (STA-98877)\n  Amount: $31,148.20 - \u2713 SUPPORTED\n\nASSESSMENT: Variance fully explained and documented. One-time data migration pushed costs up in March; underlying recurring infrastructure costs ($31,148) remained consistent with February's $31,302.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n2. TRAVEL (Account 6300)\n   February: $785.40\n   March:    $7,158.41\n   Change:   +$6,372.01 (+811.2%)\n\nDRIVERS:\n\u2022 JE-00300 (3/29/26): Travel reimbursement - T. Vance\n  Amount: $6,300.00 - \u274c NO SUPPORT DOCUMENT\n  \n\u2022 JE-00269 (3/16/26): Delta Air Lines airfare\n  Amount: $566.47 - \u2713 SUPPORTED\n  \n\u2022 JE-00266 (3/15/26): Hilton Garden Inn hotel\n  Amount: $197.45 - \u2713 SUPPORTED\n  \n\u2022 JE-00277 (3/21/26): Uber ground transport\n  Amount: $53.29 - \u2713 SUPPORTED\n  \n\u2022 JE-00298 (3/27/26): Uber ground transport\n  Amount: $41.20 - \u2713 SUPPORTED\n\nASSESSMENT: \u274c DOES NOT HOLD UP. The $6,300 travel reimbursement (JE-00300, manual entry) comprises 88% of the monthly variance but lacks supporting documentation. The remaining travel expenses ($857.41) represent normal business travel activity. The unsupported reimbursement requires immediate attention\u2014need expense report and approval documentation for T. Vance's travel.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n3. MARKETING PROGRAMS (Account 6400)\n   February: $7,898.14\n   March:    $29,686.00\n   Change:   +$21,787.86 (+275.8%)\n\nDRIVERS:\n\u2022 JE-00241 (3/6/26): Meridian Events - SaaS Connect Spring sponsorship/event (ME-0588)\n  Event dates: 3/17-3/19\n  Amount: $22,000.00 - \u2713 SUPPORTED\n  \n\u2022 JE-00243 (3/6/26): Oakridge Creative - content and campaign services (OAK-10546)\n  Amount: $7,686.00 - \u2713 SUPPORTED\n\nASSESSMENT: Variance fully explained and documented. March saw two strategic marketing initiatives: a $22,000 industry event sponsorship and $7,686 in professional content services. These are one-time campaigns not expected to recur at this level in subsequent months.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nCONCLUSION\nTwo of the three material variances hold up completely. However, the Travel category has a critical documentation issue:\n\nACTION REQUIRED: Obtain and attach supporting documentation for JE-00300 ($6,300 travel reimbursement to T. Vance) immediately. Without this, the travel variance is partially unsupported."}, "is_error": false, "result": {"status": "memo submitted; task complete"}, "ms": 10}
